'''Aleix Riera''' (born April 18, 1999), known by his in-game handle '''Tempesta''', is a Balboan professional [[esports]] player and streamer. Widely regarded as one of the greatest ''[[Galactic Combat]]'' players of all time, Riera holds the record for most [[Galactic Combat World Championship]] (GCWC) titles by an individual player, with seven championships across two organisations. In 2026, he retired from competitive ''Galactic Combat'' and transitioned to ''[[Aterratge d'Herois]]'' (ADH), a multiplayer FPS survival game, where he won the [[ADH Grand Championship]] in 2025 and finished as runner-up in 2026.

== Early life ==

Aleix Riera was born on April 18, 1999, in [[Varakí]], Estret, [[Balboa]]. His parents were administrative staff for the [[Adonian Community]], and the family's connection to international institutions exposed Riera to a cosmopolitan environment from a young age. He developed an interest in video games early in his childhood and became known in Balboan gaming circles for his exceptional mechanical skill and reflexes.

== Career ==

=== Correcamins (2015–2022) ===

Riera began his competitive career in 2015 when he and fellow Balboan player [[Julio Nakayama]] formed the team [[Correcamins (esports)|Correcamins]] with three other players to compete in the inaugural [[Galactic Combat World Championship|GCWC]]. Riera quickly established himself as the team's star player, known for his aggressive, carry-oriented playstyle and individual playmaking ability. Under his leadership, Correcamins became the dominant team of the early GCWC era, winning championships in 2015, 2016, 2018, and 2020.

=== Força (2022–2026) ===

In 2022, Riera and Nakayama were recruited to the newly formed superteam [[Força (esports)|Força]], backed by [[Abyala Telecom]] and [[BalboaVisió]]. The move brought together two of Correcamins' star players into a roster of top talent from across multiple competitive regions. Riera continued to excel as Força's highest-rated player, and the team won three consecutive GCWC titles in [[2023 Galactic Combat World Championship|2023]], [[2024 Galactic Combat World Championship|2024]], and [[2025 Galactic Combat World Championship|2025]], remaining undefeated in international competition throughout Riera's tenure.

During this period, tensions between Riera and Nakayama intensified over opposing competitive philosophies. Riera favoured a carry-oriented strategy built around his individual playmaking, while Nakayama advocated for a more coordinated, team-based approach. The conflict culminated in Nakayama's departure from Força in early 2024. Following Nakayama's exit, Riera remained with Força and continued the team's dominance through the 2025 season.

In 2026, Riera announced his retirement from competitive ''Galactic Combat'', citing waning motivation and a desire to pursue a new competitive challenge. His departure was regarded as a significant setback for Força ahead of the [[2026 Galactic Combat World Championship]].

=== Aterratge d'Herois (2025–present) ===

While still competing in ''Galactic Combat'', Riera began playing ''[[Aterratge d'Herois]]'' (ADH), a multiplayer FPS survival game, in 2025. He quickly rose to prominence in the ADH competitive scene and won the [[ADH Grand Championship]] that same year, achieving the rare feat of holding world titles in two different games simultaneously. Following his retirement from ''Galactic Combat'' in 2026, Riera became a full-time ADH player and streamer. He finished as runner-up in the 2026 ADH Grand Championship.

Riera's transition from ''Galactic Combat'' to ADH drew significant attention from the esports community, with analysts noting that his mechanical skill and aggressive playstyle translated effectively to the FPS survival format.

